---
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import DocumentTitleBlock from '../../components/DocumentTitleBlock.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../../lib/site-config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy — ${siteConfig.eventTitle}`}
  description="What is and isn't publicly displayed, precise Capture coordinates, identifiable-people guidance, and what media removal can and cannot change."
>
  <main id="main" data-document>
    <DocumentTitleBlock>
      <Fragment slot="title">Privacy and decentralized storage</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="lead">
        <p>
          Read this page before installing Proofmode or submitting media. It is the canonical list of what the
          Public submission map does and does not display, and the full guidance on identifiable people and
          sensitive content.
        </p>
      </Fragment>
    </DocumentTitleBlock>

    <div class="doc-body">
      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="not-public">
        <h2 id="not-public">What is not public</h2>
        <p>The Public submission map does not display:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Participant names</li>
          <li>Phone numbers</li>
          <li>Email addresses</li>
          <li>Other direct personal details collected for authentication</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="may-be-public">
        <h2 id="may-be-public">What may be public</h2>
        <p>The Public submission map may display:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The full Wallet address associated with the Attestation</li>
          <li>The Capture coordinates recorded by Proofmode</li>
          <li>Raw Proofset metadata used in the Public submission map details pane</li>
          <li>Media for Approved Submissions, shown as Observations</li>
          <li>Submission and review status</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This is pseudonymous public participation, not absolute anonymity. A Wallet address is a persistent,
          pseudonymous public identifier. It is not a participant&rsquo;s name, but it may link multiple Submissions
          made with the same Wallet address.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="coordinates">
        <h2 id="coordinates">Precise Capture coordinates</h2>
        <div class="notice-slot">
          <Callout intent="privacy">
            <p>
              Precise Capture coordinates are not generalized and may be public. When a Submission is eligible for
              Public submission map display, it is shown at the coordinates recorded at Capture time. Precision
              depends on the device&rsquo;s GPS accuracy at that time.
            </p>
          </Callout>
        </div>
        <p>
          Submissions outside the campus boundary are filtered from Public submission map display by the
          event&rsquo;s backend geospatial logic.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="sensitive-content">
        <h2 id="sensitive-content">Identifiable people and sensitive content</h2>
        <p>
          Avoid photographing identifiable people, children, private situations, identification documents, license
          plates, or other sensitive information. Participants are responsible for considering the consequences of
          submitting media to a decentralized network.
        </p>
        <p>Every Submission is reviewed before its media is displayed publicly.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="decentralized-storage">
        <h2 id="decentralized-storage">Decentralized storage</h2>
        <div class="notice-slot">
          <Callout intent="irreversible">
            <p>
              On-chain Attestations are intended to remain indefinitely. An on-chain Attestation cannot be removed
              by unpinning associated media or hiding a Submission from the Public submission map.
            </p>
            <p>
              Event media is stored on IPFS. The organizer plans to pin media on its IPFS node for at least two to
              three months after the event ends. After organizer pinning ends, continued retrieval is not
              guaranteed unless other IPFS nodes retain the content. Unpinning media from the organizer&rsquo;s node
              does not guarantee that copies held elsewhere have been removed.
            </p>
          </Callout>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="removal">
        <h2 id="removal">Requesting media removal</h2>
        <p>
          To request removal of media from the organizer-controlled IPFS node and the Public submission map,
          contact the event team through <a href="/help/#official-contact">Help</a>.
        </p>
        <div class="notice-slot">
          <Callout intent="irreversible">
            <p>
              If the request is approved, the team unpins the media from the organizer&rsquo;s IPFS node and
              blacklists the Attestation from the Public submission map, so the media is not displayed there. The
              on-chain Attestation remains. Copies of the media retained by other IPFS nodes may remain accessible,
              and the event team cannot guarantee network-wide deletion.
            </p>
          </Callout>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  main#main[data-document] {
    max-width: 1760px;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .doc-body {
    padding: 48px 48px 84px;
  }

  .doc-section {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg, 2rem);
  }

  .doc-section:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .notice-slot {
    margin: var(--space-sm, 1rem) 0 var(--space-md, 1.5rem);
  }

  h2 {
    max-width: 74ch;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm, 1rem);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  p,
  ul {
    max-width: 74ch;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-2);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm, 1rem);
  }

  p:last-child,
  ul:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  ul {
    padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .doc-body {
      padding: 32px 18px 56px;
    }
  }
</style>
